{
  "title": "AddToShoppingListSheet shows success even when Core Data save \
fails",
  "description": "`Ramekin/AddToShoppingListSheet.swift:102-123` calls \
`ShoppingListStore.shared.addItemsFromRecipe(...)` and unconditionally flips \
`showingConfirmation = true`. `addItemsFromRecipe` returns Void and silently \
swallows Core Data save failures (see `saveContext` error handling). The user \
sees the green check and the sheet dismisses whether or not the items were \
actually persisted. Make `addItemsFromRecipe` throw, catch in the sheet, and \
show an error state (parallel to `AddToMealPlanSheet`'s error handling).",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 3,
  "type": "task",
  "labels": [
    "ios",
  ],
  "created_at": "2026-04-17T12:00:00-07:00",
  "updated_at": "2026-04-17T12:00:00-07:00",
}
